# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in your own values (never commit real ids of
# private projects if you don't want them public — note a Google OAuth *client
# id* is a public identifier by design; there is no client secret in this app).

# Google OAuth 2.0 "Web application" client id used by the cloud storage
# module. The repository preview already has a public development client in
# `.env.development`; set this in `.env.local` to override it with your own.
# Create one in Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services →
# Credentials, add your site origin (e.g. http://localhost:5173) to the
# Authorized JavaScript origins, and enable the Google Drive API.
#
# Which scopes to add to the OAuth consent screen depends on the provider's
# `access` option. The preview's Asset Hub browses folders the user already
# filled, so it uses `access: 'read_all'` and needs both drive.readonly and
# drive.file — drive.readonly is a restricted scope and requires verification
# for a public production app. An app that only reads back its own files
# should use the default `access: 'app_files'`, which needs drive.file alone
# and no verification. See README → "Asset Hub — cloud drive viewer" and
# "Cloud storage without the Asset Hub".
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Optional: Google API key handed to the Drive folder picker. The picker
# usually works with the OAuth token alone; set this if Google rejects the
# dialog with a developer-key error. Restrict the key to the Picker API.
# VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Optional: overrides the `app_id` the host passes to load_cloud_config().
# It namespaces the browser-local keys (access token, granted folder), so two
# apps on one origin never share a session. The preview app uses `ui`.
# VITE_CLOUD_APP_ID=ui

# Optional: folder name suggested in the picker prompt. Defaults to the
# host's root_folder_name, then to the app id. The preview app uses asset_hub.
# VITE_CLOUD_ROOT_FOLDER=asset_hub
